A||||3||Matthew_Fiero||seat trouble||||1||
Z||000000||Matthew_Fiero||09-01-2001||03:03 PM||||My Driver side seat will not move back and forth. It has been this way ever since owning it (almost 2 months) Is there a way i can fix this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||09-01-2001||03:12 PM||||Probably some corrosion on the rails.  There are four nuts that unbolt the seat from the floor.  If they are not corroded in place, remove them and the seat comes out and you can turn it over to see the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero_hunter85||09-01-2001||04:45 PM||||you might want to spray some knocker loose penatrating (sp?) fluid on the nuts before you try to take them off so you dont brake the studs. my old 88 fiero  was the same way and i took the seat out and sprayed it down real good with wd40 every 2 hours then after the 5th time i hit the seat brackets with a hammer and then it worked fine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||09-01-2001||05:38 PM||||The front-rear seat adjustment lever works one side (Door side). The other side is operated by a wire from there to the lever on the console side. Sometimes that wire will break and leave the console side locked. A bit of creativity with a coat hanger will free it so you can get to the bolts that allow you to remove the seat and repair it properly.<BR>Good Luck  ||||reg||1
